 your own draft and explain the change. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Name a specific strength (clue/goal), ask about a unclear beat, suggest one linked improvement. Reasoning: I used peer feedback by attending to kind rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Only praising or only listing faults without a next step is less useful for revision. Correction: Name a specific strength (clue/goal), ask about a unclear beat, suggest one linked improvement. Why: the correction restores accurate use of peer feedback.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Only praising or only listing faults without a next step is less useful for revision. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating peer feedback on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with peer feedback, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Name a specific strength (clue/goal), ask about a unclear beat, suggest one linked improvement. This matches the lesson skill for peer feedback.","options":["Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Name a specific strength (clue/goal), ask about a unclear beat, suggest one linked improvement.","Only praising or only listing faults without a next step is less useful for revision.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Rewrite \"I liked it\" into feedback with one strength, one 